1. create Database and EC2 instance in AWS
2. Connect EC2 to Mobaxterm
3. Update the server and install mysql-client
sudo apt-get update -y
sudo apt-get install mysql-client


4. Check if any database is running in local
mysql - u root -p
(Default username and password: root)

5. Connect RDS to EC2
mysql -u admin -h database-2.cduswyuyk9eh.ap-south-1.rds.amazonaws.com -P 3306 -p
above details can be found in RDS -> Database -> connectivity -> Endpoints
(give password created in RDS database)


6. If not connecting, then go to database -> connectivity -> set up EC2 connection (ec2-to-rds-demo server) -> Setup
7. then reboot server
sudo reboot


----------
2nd Method to connect rds to ec2
-> Go to IAM -> create roles -> AWS service -> EC2 -> Next -> AmazonRDSFullAccess, CloudWatchEventsFullAccess -> Next -> Name: ec2-to-access-rds -> create role

Now go to EC2 -> select (ec2-to-rds-demo) -> Actions -> Security -> Modify IAM Role -> attach (rds role) -> Save

Now try connecting database

mysql -u admin -h database-2.cduswyuyk9eh.ap-south-1.rds.amazonaws.com -P 3306 -p


-> It will connect

-----------------------------

show databases;
create database aws;
show databases;

use aws
CREATE TABLE learners (learner_id INT, learner_name VARCHAR(50));
select * from learners;
insert into learners (learner_id, learner_name) values(1,"Juhi");

select * from learners;

delete from learners where learner_id=1;
select * from learners;


